findings=[{
 "ref":"F-140",
 "title":"MegaETH portal upgraders can emit a deposit whose sender is the PoolManager, and mega-evm runs deposits through op-revm without nonce or code checks",
 "chainIds":[4326],"lens":"L2","assumptions":["A8","A6"],"effect":"siphon","actor":"governance","severity":"high",
 "difference":"On Ethereum only a key or the contract's own code can move what a contract holds. On MegaETH the from field of a deposit transaction is whatever the OptimismPortal2 proxy 0x7f82f57F0Dd546519324392e408b01fcC7D709e8 on Ethereum writes into TransactionDeposited. The proxy is upgradeable: its EIP-1967 admin slot holds the ProxyAdmin 0x15fcb0120d414f246ead019ca4bdf97447cd8d90, whose owner is the Safe 0x92e0e0b15e3e99b32c9ed9ad284f939553c7b7d6 with threshold 6 of 10 owners. mega-evm v1.7.4 delegates validate_against_state_and_deduct_caller to op-revm at revision f67d87cd, and op-revm returns from the deposit branch after adding the mint and bumping the nonce, without the nonce and code validation that every other transaction gets.",
 "mechanism":"The verified implementation 0x55400445e384393f9c1be23e7e734e8d44ed9fd9 (OptimismPortal2, version 3.15.2, Sourcify full match) sets from to msg.sender and replaces it with msg.sender plus 0x1111000000000000000000000000000000001111 unless msg.sender equals tx.origin or carries a 23 byte EIP-7702 delegation (OptimismPortal2.sol lines 481 to 484, EOA.sol lines 9 to 24). It only refuses the MegaETH system address 0xA887dCB9D5f39Ef79272801d05Abdf707CFBbD1d as from (line 487). An ordinary account cannot make from equal the PoolManager 0xacb7e78fa05d562e0a5d3089ec896d57d057d38e: on Ethereum that address has no code and nonce 0, and its alias preimage 0x9ba6e78fa05d562e0a5d3089ec896d57d057c27d has no code and nonce 0, so producing either would need a key or a CREATE2 preimage for a fixed 160 bit target. The proxy admin can install another implementation, as OP Mainnet governance did on 2026-10-31 (F-140), and emit TransactionDeposited with from set to the PoolManager, to set to a pooled token and calldata transfer(recipient, balance). mega-evm would run it as an outer call from the PoolManager: op-revm loads the caller, adds the mint, bumps the nonce and returns at handler.rs lines 113 to 143, and mega-evm's own before_run hook treats only transactions from the system address specially (execution.rs lines 87 to 157). The token sees an ordinary transfer by its holder. Nothing in the PoolManager runs: unlock (src/PoolManager.sol:104-114), the debit in take (src/PoolManager.sol:291-297) and the NonzeroDeltaCount check never execute, so pool state and ERC-6909 claims (src/ERC6909.sol:17) keep balances that are gone. A forged call that targets the PoolManager itself gains nothing: unlock calls unlockCallback on the PoolManager, which has no such function, and every entry point other than unlock, sync, the ERC-6909 functions and the owner functions requires the lock (src/PoolManager.sol:96-99).",
 "impact":"Every balance the PoolManager holds on MegaETH, in native ETH and in every ERC-20. Liquidity providers and claim holders would keep records that cannot be paid out. No such deposit has happened: the PoolManager's nonce on MegaETH is 1 at block 0x1f50bdd, and a deposit from it would have bumped the nonce.",
 "preconditions":"Six of the ten owners of Safe 0x92e0e0b15e3e99b32c9ed9ad284f939553c7b7d6 on Ethereum sign an upgrade of the portal through ProxyAdmin 0x15fcb0120d414f246ead019ca4bdf97447cd8d90. No ordinary account can do this.",
 "mitigations":"Treat the MegaETH portal upgrade key as custodian of every pooled balance. Liquidity providers can watch Upgraded events on 0x7f82f57F0Dd546519324392e408b01fcC7D709e8 and TransactionDeposited events whose from topic is the PoolManager. The deployer cannot close it in src: a call from the PoolManager address to a token bypasses all PoolManager code.",
 "coreRefs":["src/PoolManager.sol:104-114","src/PoolManager.sol:291-297","src/types/Currency.sol:40-80"],
 "sources":[
  {"url":MP,"supports":"Verified OptimismPortal2 source of implementation 0x55400445e384393f9c1be23e7e734e8d44ed9fd9: from is msg.sender, aliased unless EOA.isSenderEOA() (lines 481-484); MEGA_SYSTEM_ADDRESS refused as from (lines 84 and 487); TransactionDeposited emitted with that from (line 496). EOA.sol lines 9-24 accept msg.sender == tx.origin or a 23 byte 0xEF0100 delegation."},
  {"url":"https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com","supports":"Saved in "+WD+"megaportal.json. eth_getStorageAt and eth_call on Ethereum via reth/v2.11.0-b9abbcc at block 0x19444c0: implementation slot 0x55400445..., admin slot 0x15fcb012..., ProxyAdmin owner 0x92e0e0b1... with getThreshold 6 and ten owners, version 3.15.2, paused false; PoolManager address and its alias preimage have no code and nonce 0 on Ethereum; implementation bytecode contains the alias offset and the 0xEF0100 constant."},
  {"url":MEGA+"crates/mega-evm/src/evm/execution.rs","supports":"Lines 87-157: before_run promotes only transactions from the system address and whitelists their callee. Lines 581-593: validate_against_state_and_deduct_caller is delegated to op-revm."},
  {"url":MEGA+"Cargo.toml","supports":"op-revm pinned to ethereum-optimism/optimism rev f67d87cd5c9992b62d215c043917b94e3f019629 (line 140)."},
  {"url":OPR,"supports":"Lines 113-143: the deposit branch adds the mint, bumps the nonce and returns before validate_account_nonce_and_code_with_components, which only non-deposit transactions reach (line 154)."},
  {"url":"https://mainnet.megaeth.com/rpc","supports":"Saved in "+WD+"pm_nonces.json. eth_getTransactionCount of the PoolManager on MegaETH (mega-reth/v2.3.1-4499c42) at block 0x1f50bdd is 1."}],
 "evidence":"primary"}]

